    <string name="sensitivity_help_title">Calibrating sensitivity</string>
    <string name="sensitivity_help_intro">Sensitivity controls how strict cry matching is — it directly changes how many votes a candidate needs to count as a match.</string>
    <string name="sensitivity_help_strict">• Lower (Strict): needs a cleaner, closer match. Fewer false positives, but may miss quieter or noisier cries.</string>
    <string name="sensitivity_help_lenient">• Higher (Lenient): matches more readily. Catches faint or noisy cries, but may occasionally misidentify or show more possible outcomes.</string>
    <string name="sensitivity_help_tip">If you keep getting \"no Pokémon recognized\" in a noisy arcade, try raising sensitivity. If you\'re getting wrong matches, try lowering it.</string>
